    "rationale": "The whole modern English/German lexical base system recurs in independently attested French, Spanish, Italian and Russian loans from Greek systēma through Latin or French mediation. This is a recommendation based on the whole international lexical row, not shortest substring selection. systema keeps the longer full source noun form rather than the compact modern international head; this recommendation is not a general Greek/Latin ending-removal rule. syst and sys cut recognizability. Greek/Latin systemat- in derivations must be modeled as a branch stem, not a reason to invent substring membership. Preserve both ped under-stripping and creat over-stripping controls.",
